# --- PLATO: temporarily excluded, not yet a real submodule -----------------
# It has no fork we control yet, so it cannot be registered as a submodule --
# a submodule commit must be fetchable from ITS OWN remote, and the fixes in
# docs/plato_portability_fixes.patch only exist locally (see PLATO/, branch
# chemist-patches). Once a fork exists:
#   1. remove this ignore rule
#   2. inside PLATO/: git remote set-url origin <fork-url> && git push origin chemist-patches:main
#   3. from the root: git submodule add <fork-url> PLATO
/PLATO/
